Subject: [PATCH 0015] fuse GAMG finest correction addition and residual
 restriction

Let scale optionally add the updated correction to psi in its final loop.
Only the finest Vcycle call supplies psi; coarse-level scaling retains the
original loop via a null default argument. Keep the literal scaling expression
sf*field[i] + (source[i] - sf*Acf[i])/D[i], store it to field[i], then execute
the original psi[i] += field[i]. The scale-factor dot products, cell order,
MPI reduction, stabilisation, Amul, debug output and Jacobi update are
unchanged. No addition is folded algebraically into the scaling expression.
When scaleCorrection=false, keep the original standalone addition loop.
No additional fusion is attempted on coarse corrections that must be smoothed
before prolongation.

After each Vcycle, when another cycle is permitted by min/max iteration
limits and level 0 has no processor gather, combine finestResidual=source-Apsi
with restriction into coarseSources[0]. Keep the stored residual for exactly
the same gSumMag, scaling and setResidualField hooks. Use the same positive
zero initialization and resize as restrictField, and for i in ascending fine
cell order execute coarse[addr[i]] += finestResidual[i]. Each residual is the
same scalar subtraction on the same operands. Each coarse sum sees identical
rounded values in precisely the same sequence as GAMGAgglomeration's original
restrictField. There is no multiplication here to introduce an FMA across the
new addition. The next Vcycle skips only the already completed restriction.

The first Vcycle still uses the original restriction; the final iteration
limit avoids unused restriction. If an earlier convergence check succeeds,
its prepared local coarse field is simply discarded. The convergence check,
iteration counters, norms and number/order of reductions remain unchanged.
With a processor gather at level 0 use subtract plus the original restrictField
in Vcycle, so communication and gather order are untouched. All deeper-level
restriction is unchanged. In particular, do not substitute Amul plus a new
subtraction for the pre-smoothing residual method: that would change the
per-cell accumulation/rounding order.

Official occDrivAerStaticMesh fvSolution: p=GAMG/GaussSeidel, maxIter=12,
tolerance=relTol=0, coarsestLevelCorr=PCG/DIC with minIter=maxIter=35.
The default controls enable scaleCorrection for this symmetric pressure
matrix, nPreSweeps=0 and interpolateCorrection=false. No case dictionaries,
coarsest PCG code or sweep/iteration counts change.

For a 12-cycle solve without a level-0 processor gather, remove 12 standalone
finest-grid addition passes and merge 11 residual/restriction passes over
~65.3M cells globally (~127.5k/rank at 512 ranks). The same coarse zero fills
and all coarse sums remain. Estimate ~4-6/2396 profile samples (0.17-0.25%):
parts of scale's 17 self samples, Vcycle's 4 self samples and restriction's
5 non-memset samples; neither its 3 memset samples nor MPI/Amul time is claimed.
This estimate is not a measured speedup.

Validation: GCC 13.3 -fsyntax-only with check-all.sh flags/includes passes
GAMGSolverSolve.C, GAMGSolverScale.C, GAMGSolver.C and GAMGSolverInterpolate.C.
A standalone GCC -O3 -march=native -ffp-contract=fast probe compares 4,031,568
values bitwise for separate vs fused scaling/addition and residual/restriction,
including signed zero, cancellation, wide exponent ranges and empty fields.
All match. EPYC znver3 assembly generation with contraction enabled also
succeeds and contains FMA instructions. This supplements the per-value proof;
the owner still needs the full serial/MPI coefficient.dat identity run.
